homelab-roundcube (0.1.7) unstable; urgency=medium

  * recipient_blocking: fix a real, reproducible failure of every AJAX
    action (block/unblock/list) found only by an actual end-to-end
    browser-session test, not by inspection -- Debian's roundcube-core
    ships no vendor/autoload.php; GuzzleHttp\Client is only ever loaded
    within a request by rcmail_oauth.php's own conditional include, and
    only when that file's code actually runs (e.g. IMAP/SMTP connection
    setup), never guaranteed for a plugin's own standalone action. Now
    loads Guzzle itself the same way, and logs (rather than silently
    swallowing) any \Throwable from the API call
  * recipient_blocking: add one bounded retry for pure transport-level
    API failures -- php-fpm here has no `curl` extension loaded, so
    Guzzle falls back to its plain PHP-stream handler (no connection
    pooling/retry of its own); confirmed by repeated live testing this
    occasionally hits a bare ECONNREFUSED against homelab-api under this
    environment's real concurrent load even though the very next attempt
    succeeds. A real 4xx/5xx response is never retried, only a true
    transport failure (no response at all)

 -- Gardner <gardner@homelab>  Sat, 12 Sep 2026 13:42:19 -0500

homelab-roundcube (0.1.5) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Add recipient_blocking plugin: block/unblock one of your own
    addresses from the message toolbar and Settings; calls homelab-api's
    existing self-service recipient-access API using the same JWT
    already used for IMAP/SMTP, no new credential
  * postinst: symlink the new plugin into /var/lib/roundcube/plugins/
    (Debian's roundcube-core resolves plugins there, not directly under
    /usr/share/roundcube/plugins/ where the package installs them) --
    without this every page request 500s with "Failed to load plugin
    file"; postrm removes the symlink on package removal

 -- Gardner <gardner@homelab>  Sat, 12 Sep 2026 13:35:43 -0500

